{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "4: Configure CIBA in Auth0",
  "nextTour": "5: Add Human-in-the-Loop Authorization",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "What is CIBA?",
      "description": "## What is CIBA?\n\n**Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication (CIBA)** is an OAuth 2.0 extension that allows a client (the AI agent) to request authorization from a user through an **out-of-band channel** — for example, a push notification to their phone.\n\nUnlike regular OAuth flows where the user is redirected to a browser, CIBA works like this:\n\n1. Z-Assistant detects that a **sensitive operation** is requested (e.g., a refund).\n2. The `withRefundApproval` wrapper intercepts the tool call and initiates a CIBA request to Auth0.\n3. Auth0 sends a **push notification** to the user's registered device (Auth0 Guardian app).\n4. The notification shows: _\"Approve refund of $216.99 for order ORD-1001?\"_\n5. The user taps **Approve** or **Deny** on their phone.\n6. If approved, Z-Assistant executes the refund. If denied, it returns an authorization error.\n\nThis is **human-in-the-loop** authorization for AI agents."
    },
    {
      "title": "Install Auth0 Guardian",
      "description": "## Install Auth0 Guardian\n\nAuth0 Guardian is the mobile app that receives CIBA push notifications.\n\n1. Install **Auth0 Guardian** on your phone:\n   - [iOS App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/auth0-guardian/id1093100804)\n   - [Google Play Store](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.auth0.guardian)\n\n2. We will enroll your account with Guardian after enabling CIBA on your tenant.\n\n> If you don't have a smartphone, Auth0 also supports email and SMS as CIBA notification channels. Check the Auth0 documentation for setup instructions."
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable CIBA on your Auth0 Tenant",
      "description": "## Enable CIBA on your Auth0 Tenant\n\nCIBA is a tenant-level feature that must be explicitly enabled.\n\n1. In the [Auth0 Dashboard](https://manage.auth0.com), go to **Security → Attack Protection**.\n2. Select the **Bot Detection** section — CIBA is found in **Advanced Settings**.\n\nActually, CIBA is configured under a different path. Follow these steps:\n\n1. Go to **Auth0 Dashboard → Applications → APIs**.\n2. Select **Auth0 Management API** → **Settings** tab.\n3. Scroll to **OIDC Backchannel Logout** — this is where CIBA is configured.\n\n**Correct path:**\n1. Go to **Auth0 Dashboard → Tenant Settings** → **Advanced** tab.\n2. Scroll to find the **Backchannel Authentication** section.\n3. Toggle **Enable CIBA** to on.\n4. Save changes.\n\n> If you don't see CIBA settings, ensure your Auth0 tenant is on a plan that supports it (Developer Pro or above).",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 4
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 36
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable Push Notifications on your application",
      "description": "## Enable Push Notifications on your application\n\nYour Z-Assistant Auth0 application needs to support CIBA grant types.\n\n1. In the Auth0 Dashboard, go to **Applications → Applications** and select **Z-Assistant**.\n2. Select the **Settings** tab.\n3. Scroll to **Advanced Settings → Grant Types**.\n4. Enable **CIBA** (it may appear as `urn:openid:params:grant-type:ciba`).\n5. Save changes.\n\nAlso confirm that **Client Credentials** is enabled — Auth0 AI uses it internally when making CIBA requests."
    },
    {
      "title": "Configure a Push Notification factor",
      "description": "## Configure a Push Notification factor\n\nFor CIBA to deliver approval notifications, you need to configure a notification channel.\n\n**Recommended: Auth0 Guardian push notifications**\n\n1. In the Auth0 Dashboard, go to **Security → Multi-Factor Auth**.\n2. Ensure **Push Notifications** (Guardian) is enabled.\n3. Save.\n\nYour account also needs to be enrolled in Guardian:\n\n1. Start Z-Assistant and log in.\n2. Go to your Auth0 Universal Login profile or your tenant's user management.\n3. Enroll your account in **Guardian Push Notifications**.\n\nAlternatively, you can set up the Guardian app during first login by enabling the required MFA policy on your Auth0 tenant."
    },
    {
      "title": "Verify your setup",
      "description": "## Verify your setup\n\nBefore writing code, confirm everything is configured:\n\n- [ ] CIBA is enabled on your Auth0 tenant\n- [ ] The Z-Assistant application has the CIBA grant type enabled\n- [ ] Auth0 Guardian push notifications are enabled\n- [ ] Your user account is enrolled in Guardian\n\nWith these settings in place, Auth0's CIBA endpoint is ready to receive authorization requests from Z-Assistant and route approval notifications to your device.\n\nIn the next tour, we'll add the CIBA authorization wrappers to the sensitive tools in code."
    }
  ]
}